  "body": "I'm looking at implementing the 2dcontext currentTransform attribute. I have a question about the wording in the specification. In particular:\n\n\"When the transformation matrix is mutated by the methods described in this section, the last DOMMatrix object to which the attribute has been set must be mutated in a corresponding fashion.\"\n\nThe way I read this implies that if I have a reference to the DOMMatrix of currentTransform, and then call scale() directly on the context object, my DOMMatrix should update. Is this correct?\n\nIf not, then I'm happy. If it is correct, then I wonder why :)\n\nMozilla's prototype of this, mozCurrentTransform, is not live, but it is an Array rather than a DOMMatrix. \n",
